cheese lovers guys let's talk about  booze I love my cocktails but what I  don't love is the double whammy sugar  and booze hangover that you get from  super boozy sugary drinks oh it's not  good so that's why I developed a little  technique that I call balanced boozing  that basically involves going easy on  the liquor in my cocktails avoiding the  super sugary drinks and having a few  sips of water between each sip of  alcohol so today I'm going to share with  you three of my favorite fall cocktails  to help you get through those holidays  even with crazy Uncle Bill let's get  started first up is my own my pumpkin  chai cocktail first I bring some water  to a boil in a small saucepan and add in  some diced pear maple syrup pumpkin  puree ginger pumpkin pie spice and lemon  juice cover and simmer for about five  minutes  then turn off the heat add in the chai  tea bag and vanilla and let it sit until  fully cooled using a slotted spoon  remove all of the pear ginger and tea  bits and then set that aside then to  make the cocktail I add one else at the  Bourbon and one and a half ounces of the  pumpkin syrup to a mixer with some ice  shake until well chilled then strain  into a cup top with a little bit of club  soda and garnish with a piece of candy  ginger next is my apple pie mimosa I  start by lightly wetting the rim of a  champagne flute and dipping it into some  ground cinnamon then I put two ounces of  apple cider into each champagne flute  and top it off with three ounces of  sparkling wine garnish with a slice of  apple and enjoy finally my apple and  cranberry kombucha sangria in a large  pitcher I mix together one ball of white  wine two cups of ginger kombucha sliced  Apple sliced lemon and some  frozen cranberries pug eyes it's 5 p.m.  somewhere and I am ready to drink up  seriously these are my favorite videos  to shoot like like we need to write more  of these kinds of videos like every  single week so just just put that in the  calendar ok I hope you enjoyed my fall  cocktail video if you did give me the  thumbs up leave me a comment below with  what you're gonna be drinking this  holiday season and maybe I'll lighten it  up for you subscribe to the channel and  I'll see you next time on Abbey's  kitchen
 

